# Telegram bot

## Access model

- Bot API only — not MTProto / user-account clients.
- Long polling via `getUpdates`. Offset tracking = Telegram's `update_id`.
- The bot must be added to the single target group; listen to that group only.

## Implementation

- Use `python-telegram-bot`'s `Bot` class only (see tech-stack rule).
- Own asyncio loop + offset persistence; do not use `Application` / handlers.
- Listener responsibilities: validate URLs, quick accept/reject reply, enqueue accepted jobs.

## Known limitation (document in code comments when touching this)

`getUpdates` only returns unacknowledged updates (Telegram buffers ~24h). It cannot fetch arbitrary chat history. State-file loss beyond that window is unrecoverable via this API — reconciliation can prevent reprocessing, but cannot recover missed messages older than the buffer.
